## WonderLantern org — the direct predecessor

The `WonderLantern` organisation publishes the work this repository follows.
Their Z6 project is the single most important reference: it targets the **same
firmware version** this toolkit analyses.

### WonderLantern/WonderLantern-z6 — Wonder Lantern Community License
<https://github.com/WonderLantern/WonderLantern-z6>
(previously reachable as `github.com/vic2349/Wonder-Lantern`)

"Nikon Z6 长曝光与肩屏倒计时 v1". Applies to the Nikon Z6 only, based on
firmware C3.80 — the same package this repository works on. It implements a
**custom shutter sound** and moves the top-plate countdown into a
card-loaded `SLOWCORE.BIN`.

This is the basis for this repository's assessment that goal 3 (custom shutter
sound on Z6 C3.80) is achievable: the stock firmware has no user-facing audio
playback path, but a card-loaded binary injected by a patch can supply one.

Their own notes record that the sound menu's touch handling is not fixed yet and
that the shutter countdown is unavailable under the mechanical shutter.

### WonderLantern/wonder-lantern-z30 — MIT (most files) + Wonder Lantern Community License (14 files)
<https://github.com/WonderLantern/wonder-lantern-z30>
(previously reachable as `github.com/RealCaCl2/z30-firmware-extensions`)

"Source-based Nikon Z30 C 1.20 firmware extensions and patch tools". The Z30 is
EXPEED 6 like the Z6.

This repository's **patch model** follows theirs:

- deliver a standalone EG module rather than a repackaged container, so the
  keyed whole-package digest is never needed;
- equal-length byte edits that must match expected stock bytes;
- code appended before the trailing CRC, four-byte aligned;
- module CRC recomputed and self-checked to residue 0;
- reuse of the stock 16:9 slot for custom aspect ratios.

The following files in their repository are under the separate **Wonder Lantern
